    "reading": {
        "body": "Cohere builds enterprise LLM products optimized for retrieval-augmented generation, with all three tracked offerings emphasizing data privacy and on-premises deployment control rather than scale.\n\nThe company's product line reflects a deliberate positioning away from the frontier model race. Command R+, Coral, and the API are each designed for organizations that need language models integrated into existing workflows while retaining control over their data. RAG optimization appears across all three offerings, suggesting Cohere's technical thesis prioritizes grounding models in customer-specific information over raw model capability.\n\nThis focus has implications for compute demand. RAG-native systems typically require less raw model scale because retrieval handles factuality and specificity. A customer using Command R+ with grounded data sources may need fewer parameters and less inference compute than a customer relying on a frontier model's internal knowledge. For the grid constraint, this matters: enterprise adoption driven by privacy and data control creates different power profiles than adoption driven by capability.\n\nThe data does not cover Cohere's training infrastructure, inference capacity, or actual power consumption. It does not indicate whether the company runs its own data centers or uses cloud providers. It shows what Cohere sells, not the compute or grid requirements behind those products.",
